<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pasquale Paoli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1725">1725</a>–<a href="/years/1807">1807</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pasquale Paoli was a Corsican patriot elected general of the nation in 1755. He governed the island as an independent republic under a written constitution admired across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/age-of-enlightenment">Enlightenment</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> bought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corsica">Corsica</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a> and defeated him at Ponte Novu in 1769. Returning during the Revolution, he broke with France and created the Anglo-Corsican Kingdom in 1794, dying in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pasquale-paoli.jpg" alt="Pasquale Paoli" width="320" height="431" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: William BEECHEY · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_de_Pascal_Paoli_-_William_BEECHEY.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
